* Motorola MC1350 monolithic IF amplifier -- repaired legacy macro-model.
*
* Physical pin order is preserved one-to-one:
*   1 output, 2 V+, 3 ground, 4 input, 5 AGC, 6 input, 7 ground, 8 output.
*
* The transistor-level source was archived in the user's earlier Model 249
* project and identifies SPICE modeling by Jim Thompson, 2014.  In that file
* the two output-transistor collectors were mistakenly tied to pin 2, leaving
* physical output pins 1 and 8 connected only to package capacitance.  This
* project copy reconnects those collectors to pins 1 and 8, matching the
* Motorola internal schematic and the requirement that collector voltage be
* supplied through a center-tapped coil.
*
* Statistical LOT/DEV modifiers unsupported by ngspice were removed without
* changing nominal component values.  Package parasitics remain estimates.
* Validate absolute gain and AGC response against hardware before treating
* simulated amplitudes as measured or factory performance.

